  "worked_solution": "**Method 1**\n\nThe function ${f}^{-1}(x)$ reverses the action of $f(x),$ as depicted below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14208916/assets/a0194a90466532c723c904d5ef9fea394e976b8b1f5287f066d5843f575e762e.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the above, we see that ${f}^{-1}(4)=5.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFrom the given mapping diagram, we have:\n\n$$\nf(5)=4\n$$\n\nApplying ${f}^{-1}$ to both sides of the above equation, and using the fact that ${f}^{-1}(f(x))=x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(f(5)) & ={f}^{-1}(4) \\\\ 5 & ={f}^{-1}(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that ${f}^{-1}(4)=5.$",
